   "body": "**Scope update: operator decisions, 2026-11-07** (`ext/francoisgn-suborch-1`, after the operator's device test).\n\nThe operator saw one notification for 1 to N unread MPs, and none for each new reply. That notification came from the **legacy app** (SwiftHFR has no notification code yet). Its behaviour must change in our implementation. Legacy notifies only when the home-page count of unread **conversations** goes up (`MPBackgroundService.swift:93-157` @ 2440d79), so a reply in an already-unread conversation sends nothing. Legacy also uses one fixed text and no `threadIdentifier`.\n\nNothing the operator reports goes to M5: all of the following stays in this lot (M4).\n\n**Detection**\n- The home `GET /` stays the first, cheap request.\n- On every due check, LOT-140 also fetches the MP list page 1 (`PageFetcher.privateMessages(page: 1)`). That is at most 2 requests per check, and never a thread page: a thread page would mark it read (E25).\n- A conversation is news when it is newly unread, **or** when its `repliesCount` or `lastPost` grew while it was already unread.\n- The ledger (LOT-091) needs a per-thread `repliesCount` / `lastPost` watermark for MPs. The follow-up issue is linked below.\n- The first check records the baseline silently.\n\n**Notifications**\n- One notification per conversation with news.\n  - `identifier` = `mp-<topicNumber>`, so a later reply replaces it instead of stacking.\n  - `threadIdentifier` = `mp-<topicNumber>`. This brings this part of #509 into M4.\n- A burst of more than about 5 conversations collapses into one summary.\n- **Text (operator decision):**\n  - one-to-one MP: title = the interlocutor, body = the MP's title;\n  - group MP: title = the MP's title.\n  - No message content for now.\n  - Both come from the MP list row; nothing else is fetched.\n- **Locked screen:** iOS's own \"Show Previews\" setting hides the detail. The app registers a category with `hiddenPreviewsBodyPlaceholder` = \"%u nouveaux messages privés\".\n- Interruption level `.active`, sound `.default`, never `.timeSensitive`.\n- **Tap** opens the conversation (`HFRLinkRoute.privateMessageThread`); a summary notification opens the MP list.\n- **Badge:** as legacy (`mp_badge_enabled`, the unread-conversation count).\n\n**Check interval** (operator: \"on fait avec ce qu'on a\")\n- Réglages › Notifications MP › \"Vérifier les messages\": 15 min, 30 min, 1 h, 2 h, 4 h, Jamais. Default 30 min.\n- Footer: « Au plus souvent toutes les X min. iOS décide du moment réel ; ce délai est un minimum, pas une garantie. »\n- `earliestBeginDate = now + interval`, plus the ledger's `markCheckedIfDue(minimumInterval:)` guard, shared with LOT-141.\n- No Do Not Disturb option: the app cannot read Focus, and the system already filters notifications per Focus.\n- Show « Dernière vérification : hh:mm », plus a button to iOS's notification settings.\n\n**Acceptance additions**\n- A reply in an already-unread conversation produces a notification (tested on captured list pages).\n- Two checks with no change produce nothing.\n- Locked and unlocked texts are checked on a device, including Show Previews = Never.\n- No pseudo and no subject in logs.\n\n**Capture needed** (no guessing): two MP list pages around one reply in an already-unread conversation. The capture issue is linked below.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
